#
# On the removal: authz_peers_target_from_uri's reference answer was INVERTED -- its PASS
# branch required an inbound foreign-namespace EXECUTE to be ALLOWED, which 0.8.2.2 makes
# non-conformant. go removed it rather than re-pointing it, and shipped the replacement with
# a positive control, mutation-verified both ways on live peers. Our own F51/PD-1e probe is
# therefore a DELETE, not a re-target: the vector landed, and we do not keep a second source
# of truth. (CONFORMANCE-MATRIX §3's "inconclusive by design" row for this check is retired
# with it -- and that row was itself a self-authored exculpation that measured 40 WARN / 6
# PASS when finally checked. See AGENTS.md.)
#
# core_gate_fingerprint is BYTE-IDENTICAL for the FIFTH consecutive time in this shape
# (8261a033… -- cc1970f, af8a582/fceb61f, de8f807, c1b0708, now f313028), and profile.go's
# RAW sha256 did not move either. New hard checks keep landing inside existing core
# categories. Plan around it; it has never once been the anchor that fired.
